  "releaseNotes": "WorkflowForge 2.2.0 (2026-09-15)\n\nBREAKING\n- IWorkflowExecutionContext.Services (IFoundryServices) is a new interface member. Custom IWorkflowFoundry / IWorkflowExecutionContext implementations must expose it; return new FoundryServices().\n- IWorkflowForgeLogger.IsEnabled(WorkflowForgeLogLevel) is a new interface member. Derive from the new WorkflowForgeLoggerBase to inherit an implementation.\n- IFoundryServices.DisposeAll() is a new interface member.\n- The foundry now disposes only what it owns. Reset()/Dispose() no longer dispose caller-supplied operations or middleware; register foundry-owned disposables on Services.\n- Removed the WorkflowForgeLoggers static facade, and the public PropertyNameConstants / WorkflowLogMessageConstants (now internal).\n\nAdded\n- WorkflowForgeLoggerBase: optional base class supplying a MinimumLevel-driven IsEnabled.\n- Foundry-scoped Services bag with dispose-on-lease-end semantics.\n\nFixed\n- Retried operations no longer bypass inner middleware (timeout, logging, validation, persistence were all skipped on retry).\n- LoggingMiddleware is no longer inert under default options; UseLogging() emits again and failures are always logged.\n- WorkflowTimeoutMiddleware now actually cancels the workflow instead of waiting for it to finish.\n- All extension packages ship a single netstandard2.0 asset again, so ILRepack-merged libraries and their declared dependencies can no longer disagree.\n\nMigration: https://github.com/animatlabs/workflow-forge/blob/main/docs/core/foundry-lifetime.md\nFull changelog: https://github.com/animatlabs/workflow-forge/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#220---2026-09-15",
